From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - use an 8-byte IV for rfc4309

RFC 4309 carries an 8-byte IV, and the generic rfc4309 template has an
ivsize of 8. The driver registers rfc4309(ccm(aes)) with the 16-byte
ivsize of ccm(aes), so the self-test rejects it:

  alg: aead: ivsize for ccm-aes-esp-iproc (16) doesn't match generic
  impl (8)

aead_enqueue() also copies 12 bytes of req->iv after the 3-byte salt,
which reads past an 8-byte IV. spum_ccm_update_iv() then overwrites
the last 4 of them with the length field.

Register an ivsize of CCM_ESP_IV_SIZE, and copy the ivsize of the
transform from req->iv. That is what was copied before for every
other AEAD.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -2781,8 +2781,7 @@ static int aead_enqueue(struct aead_request *req, bool is_encrypt)
 			memcpy(rctx->msg_buf.iv_ctr + ctx->salt_offset,
 			       ctx->salt, ctx->salt_len);
 		memcpy(rctx->msg_buf.iv_ctr + ctx->salt_offset + ctx->salt_len,
-		       req->iv,
-		       rctx->iv_ctr_len - ctx->salt_len - ctx->salt_offset);
+		       req->iv, crypto_aead_ivsize(aead));
 	}
 
 	rctx->chan_idx = select_channel();
@@ -3179,7 +3178,7 @@ static struct iproc_alg_s driver_algs[] = {
 			.cra_flags = CRYPTO_ALG_NEED_FALLBACK
 		 },
 		 .setkey = aead_ccm_esp_setkey,
-		 .ivsize = CCM_AES_IV_SIZE,
+		 .ivsize = CCM_ESP_IV_SIZE,
 		 .maxauthsize = AES_BLOCK_SIZE,
 	 },
 	 .cipher_info = {
